  "project_description": "Adds a filter that can be applied to text input formats to make complex regex text replacements. Configure it by visiting admin/config/content/formats, editing a text format, and enabling the Regex Text Replacement filter. Each line of the filter settings is a `pattern||replacement` pair, where `(1)`-style backreferences in the replacement are translated to `$1`. For example, `/<h[1|2]([^>]*)>(.*?)<\\/h[1|2][^>]*>/mi||<h3(1)>(2)</h3>` replaces h1/h2 tags with h3. Requires no modules outside of Drupal core (core filter). Maintained by robloach, mikemccaffrey, and yuriseki.",
